## Third-party tool licensing

CodeHealthMind does **not** vendor, link against, or copy source from the tools
it drives.  It invokes them as external command line programs and parses their
output:

| Tool      | Driven how                  | Licence            |
|-----------|-----------------------------|--------------------|
| PMD / CPD | `java -cp ... net.sourceforge.pmd.*` | BSD-style (Apache-2.0 for some modules) |
| SpotBugs | `java -jar spotbugs.jar`    | LGPL-2.1           |
| Semgrep   | `semgrep` CLI               | LGPL-2.1           |
| Knip      | `node knip.js`              | ISC                |
| javac     | `javac` from the JDK        | GPLv2 + Classpath Exception |
| OpenRewrite | Maven/Gradle plugin       | Apache-2.0         |

Because these are used as separate processes over their public CLI, their
licences do not propagate to this project.  Reference projects that informed the
*design* (Ponytail, Alibaba OpenCodeReview, open-code-review) are credited in
`docs/architecture.md`; no code was copied from them.  See
`docs/adr/ADR-002-reference-project-usage.md`.
